I can work around it by getting rid of the block, so eliminating the coverage-flag isn't a problem (but I want the block in my real code to encapsulate the &lt;C&gt;my&lt;/C&gt; variables to be private just for my &lt;C&gt;get&lt;/C&gt; function, so I'm not going to do that).  Or I can cheat with &lt;c&gt;# uncoverable statement count:2&lt;/c&gt;.  But my curiosity has been piqued as to why I should need a workaround at all.&lt;!-- Wiki2Monks {"version":1.161} --&gt;</doctext>
